From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 19:09:59 -0647
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: net: nfc: nxp,nci: Allow a reference clock

Some boards gate the controller's reference clock, or the SoC pad it
comes from, in a clock provider: the Pixel 9a's ST54L takes its clock
from a pad the PMU enables. Allow one clock.

Signed-off-by: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/nfc/nxp,nci.yaml | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/nfc/nxp,nci.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/nfc/nxp,nci.yaml
index fbf2b14f6..a1d4603a5 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/nfc/nxp,nci.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/nfc/nxp,nci.yaml
@@ -26,6 +26,11 @@ properties:
               - st,st54l
           - const: nxp,nxp-nci-i2c
 
+  clocks:
+    maxItems: 1
+    description: The controller's reference clock, or the SoC clock pad
+      that feeds it on the controller's request
+
   enable-gpios:
     description: Output GPIO pin used for enabling/disabling the controller
 
